# MESSAGE: [BC-GATE-002] two cases in one taxonomy share a caseOrder or a caseName.
#
# `bc:caseOrder` fixes emission order and `bc:caseName` becomes the Rust variant
# identifier, so a collision inside one taxonomy either silently merges two cases or
# emits a duplicate variant. The second fails at `rustc`, which is late but loud; the
# first is a silent wrong answer, because the emitted enum is simply shorter than the
# graph and nothing compares the two.
#
# Scoped per taxonomy deliberately. Distinct taxonomies routinely reuse an order and
# occasionally a name -- `bc:PddlEffect` and `bc:RefusalReason` both have a case at
# order 1 -- and that is not an error.
#
# `STR(?a) < STR(?b)` reports each colliding pair once rather than twice.
PREFIX bc: <https://bcinr.dev/ontology#>

SELECT ?taxonomy ?a ?b ?collision WHERE {
    ?a bc:inTaxonomy ?taxonomy .
    ?b bc:inTaxonomy ?taxonomy .
    FILTER(STR(?a) < STR(?b))
    {
        ?a bc:caseOrder ?collision .
        ?b bc:caseOrder ?collision .
    }
    UNION
    {
        ?a bc:caseName ?collision .
        ?b bc:caseName ?collision .
    }
}
